{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1506826-the-first-pack","id":1506826,"title":"The First Pack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-28T21:41:37-07:00","id":1506826,"title":"The First Pack","content":"Is it possible that the exarchs are really the first pack? It is said the exarchs broke reality and created the lie, the first pack killed Father Wolf and ended the way the world worked, Their magic could just be vast amounts of numenia / influence as befits the children of two of the most powerful spirits ever. <br /> <br /> I'll admit I know very little of the exarchs so this may not make any sense at all, but it makes me feel warm and fuzzy to think the Forsaken are on the top of reality instead of weird mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T23:58:59-07:00","id":1506828,"title":"","content":"Extremely unlikely. Especially with a great part of Mage's theme being that the almighty horrors that crush reality are too human, and the First Pack don't quite fit that bill.<br /> <br /> Though, I'm personally fond of the idea that The Nemesis has something to do with the Sundering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T08:49:52-07:00","id":1506854,"title":"","content":"In The Sundered World Atlantis has already been erased from existence, and the Exarchs are already in power, but the First Pack are still running with <i>Urfarah</i>, so I don't think they could be the same unless you want to retcon quite a bit.<br /> <br /> If you want to tie the Exarchs into Werewolf's cosmology, one option is to say that Urfarah wasn't just the dominant Pangaean, he is actually one of the old gods that the Exarchs exiled from the Supernal when they ascended","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T10:54:06-07:00","id":1506859,"title":"","content":"Basically, <i>The Sundered World</i> Dark Era gives you the rundown on what happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1506826-the-first-pack#post1506826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible that the exarchs are really the first pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're massively rewriting the setting, no. The Firstborn are still around, wandering the Shadow. Meanwhile, the Exarchs extend their power from their palaces in the Supernal. Frankly, they're just not very similar beyond the surface details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their magic could just be vast amounts of numenia / influence... </div> </div> </div>There <i>is </i>reference (I think) to this idea. The Bristol setting in the 2e core has <i>Afzu\u2019Umm\u2019Ia,</i> an Idigam that apparently has a practice of turning up in sea-side communities of humans and teaching them things, including arcane powers; a process which has led to tales such as Atlantis. I believe one of the writers (if not the developer) mentioned running a Forsaken game where Awakened magic descended from an Idigam. I assume these the former is the remains of the latter. Does it work? Not if you pull over all of Mage, but it's a fun idea nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...as befits the children of two of the most powerful spirits ever. </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily advertised clearly, but the Firstborn aren't children of Luna. Additionally, Father Wolf wasn't a spirit (exactly), they were a Pangaean, a third class of entities that live in the liminal space between the material and the shadow, the Pangaea that Werewolf frequently mentions. Interestingly, Pangaeans actually use the Arcana of mage.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T17:46:03-07:00","id":1506898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1506826-the-first-pack?p=1506859#post1506859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're massively rewriting the setting, no. The Firstborn are still around, wandering the Shadow.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> It's not necessarily advertised clearly, but the Firstborn aren't children of Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that it changes your point, but the First Pack were the first werewolves, not another term for the Firstborn. The Sundered World describes them in a separate paragraph from the Firstborn as ancient werewolves who have &quot;surrendered themselves so utterly to the hunt that they know nothing else.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T20:49:25-07:00","id":1506924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1506826-the-first-pack?p=1506859#post1506859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, Father Wolf wasn't a spirit (exactly), they were a Pangaean.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Father Wolf was neither spirit nor flesh, but a secret third thing.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm another person saying that the Exarchs were completely different both in type and in identity from the first wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T15:55:42-07:00","id":1506997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1506826-the-first-pack?p=1506924#post1506924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Father Wolf was neither spirit nor flesh, but a secret third thing.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm another person saying that the Exarchs were completely different both in type and in identity from the first wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pangaeans were fleshy, if not Fleshy, and it's not so much a secret anymore. That's the entire thing about The Sundered World as Pangaeans go.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;Were the Exarchs the first [were/]wolves?&quot;, <i>probably not</i>?<br /> <br /> What they are is the most discernable thing about them, which is Supernal Tyrants. The Seers posit they were humans, because they want to believe they can eat the same pie, but there's a mixture of no evidence and contradicting evidence on if they were ever anything Phenomenal, because that's the sort of shit that happens with Aponia-but the First Pack are a <i>thing</i> in the current standing world soul/timeline. If you're something that concrete and definable, odds are against you <i>also</i> an Ascended being, given the consequences that comes with just mucking about with the Supernal, nevermind joining with it.<br /> <br /> Nevermind the metaphysics of the first pack, as werewolves in extremis, really making that unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}